{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794761384,"nonce":"F+eV3nLZUo3+JY06S054PtRG8ck=","message":"First nAIR enrichment landed: call summaries (723465f0).\n\nWhat it is. `air::v2::facts`: `Function.facts` maps a callee findex to the alias classes it may write (`Footprint`, capped at 32 classes then \"anything\"). `summarize` solves it over direct calls with a worklist, so recursion settles; `attach` gives a function the summaries of what it calls; the inliner merges a callee's facts into the caller. `clobbers_all` and `writes_may_alias` take the facts, and LICM and GVN's `clobber_free` pass `f.facts`. A call with a summary blocks only the classes it may write. ash_nair solves the summaries for the functions it lowers and attaches them before `optimize`.\n\nWhy on Function and not on the instruction. About 120 sites name Call, CallMethod and CallClosure, and every other planned fact (immutable field, non-null, exact receiver) is about an entity, not an instruction. Entity-keyed facts also survive passes that move instructions.\n\nRules that hold it up (tests in air for each):\n- A summary never protects a cell load: the callee may have been handed the cell's address.\n- CallMethod, CallClosure, natives and callees outside the set are \"anything\".\n- A callee's own cells are left out of its footprint.\n- Absent facts read as the old answer, so bytecode-lowered functions are unchanged.\n\nOpen decisions:\n1. LICM may now speculate a load past a call that may throw, as it already does past NullCheck and DynGet. If a null object makes the hoisted load fault before the callee's exception, the exception that surfaces differs. Strict fix: a `may_throw` bit in the summary and a LICM rule that uses it.\n2. A field is named by the object type the writing code used, and `ObjField` of a subclass and of its base do not alias in `may_alias`. When fields are lowered, `obj_ty` must be the declaring class, or summaries across functions are unsound.\n3. Summaries are assumptions about callee bodies, like inlined bodies. Hot reload of a callee would invalidate them. The nAIR path is not connected to reload.\n\nNot shown yet: no speed number. The lowering has no fields or globals, so no lowered function has a load for the summaries to move. The numeric kernels all summarize to \"writes nothing\", which the test checks. The payoff needs field and static lowering first; until then LICM and GVN acting is shown only by the hand-built loops in air's tests.","files":null}]}